 Feasibility — 
  Yes, the project is feasible, especially when developed first as a small MVP (Minimum Viable Product). 
 The proposed MVP includes a mobile app, user registration, medical profile, emergency contacts, one custom trigger word, voice-trigger detection, SOS notification flow, live location sharing, and emergency history.
Important challenges: • Mobile operating systems may restrict continuous background microphone listening.
• Internet connectivity may not always be available during an emergency.
• Continuous voice monitoring can affect battery life. • Medical information requires strong privacy and security.
• Ambulance/emergency integration can differ by region.
SCALABILITY
Yes. The project can begin as a simple mobile emergency application and gradually become a larger emergency-response platform
Version 1 — MVP
Voice trigger → SOS → caregiver alert → GPS location
VERSION 2 Reliability 
Escalation → backup caregiver → retry/fallback mechanisms
VERSION 3 Advanced
Fall detection → wearable integration → multilingual support
Version 4 Intelligent 
 Hospital integration → smart routing → AI severity estimation
 
